The new code explicitly treats a `bytes` line as possible (`size = len(line) if isinstance(line, bytes) else ...`), but it computes `complete = line.endswith("
")` before that branch. Given a bytes-returning stream, e.g. `read_line(io.BytesIO(b"{}
"), 10)`, `line.endswith("
")` raises `TypeError` instead of returning `(b"{}
", 0)`. If the shim ever uses a binary stdin/pipe stream (the bytes branch says it may), the reader thread dies before framing or oversize handling can run.

